{"id":"mahabharata-5-164","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":164,"title":"चतुःषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 164 · Bhishma counts the great warriors","summary":{"en":"Bhishma names Shakuni, Ashvatthaman, Drona, Bahlika, Kripa, Bhagadatta and others, rating Drona and Ashvatthaman especially high, though he warns that Ashvatthaman loves his life too much, and Bhagadatta will fight like Indra on his elephant.","kn":"ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಶಕುನಿ, ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ, ದ್ರೋಣ, ಬಾಹ್ಲೀಕ, ಕೃಪ, ಭಗದತ್ತ ಮೊದಲಾದವರನ್ನು ಹೆಸರಿಸಿ ದ್ರೋಣ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮರನ್ನು ವಿಶೇಷವಾಗಿ ಎತ್ತರದಲ್ಲಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮನಿಗೆ ಜೀವದ ಮೇಲೆ ಅತಿ ಮೋಹ, ಭಗದತ್ತನು ಆನೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ಇಂದ್ರನಂತೆ ಹೋರಾಡುವನು ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म शकुनि, अश्वत्थामा, द्रोण, बाह्लीक, कृप, भगदत्त और अन्यों के नाम बताते हैं, द्रोण और अश्वत्थामा को विशेष रूप से ऊँचा आँकते हैं, यद्यपि चेताते हैं कि अश्वत्थामा को अपने प्राण अत्यधिक प्रिय हैं, और भगदत्त अपने हाथी पर इन्द्र की तरह लड़ेंगे।","te":"భీష్ముడు శకుని, అశ్వత్థామ, ద్రోణుడు, బాహ్లీకుడు, కృపుడు, భగదత్తుడు మొదలైనవారిని పేర్కొని ద్రోణుడు, అశ్వత్థామను ప్రత్యేకంగా ఉన్నతంగా అంచనా వేస్తాడు; అయితే అశ్వత్థామకు ప్రాణంపై అతి మమకారమని, భగదత్తుడు ఏనుగుపై ఇంద్రునిలా పోరాడతాడని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"பீஷ்மர் ஶகுனி, அஶ்வத்தாமா, த்ரோணர், பாஹ்லீகன், க்ருபர், பகதத்தன் முதலியோரைப் பெயரிட்டு த்ரோணரையும் அஶ்வத்தாமாவையும் சிறப்பாக உயர்வாக மதிப்பிடுகிறார்; ஆனால் அஶ்வத்தாமாவுக்கு உயிர் மீது மிகுந்த பற்று, பகதத்தன் யானை மீது இந்திரனைப் போல் போரிடுவான் என்கிறார்.","ml":"ശകുനി, അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ്, ദ്രോണർ, ബാഹ്ലികൻ, കൃപർ, ഭഗദത്തൻ എന്നിവരെയും മറ്റുള്ളവരെയും ഭീഷ്മർ പേരെടുത്ത് പറയുന്നു; ദ്രോണരെയും അശ്വത്ഥാമാവിനെയും പ്രത്യേകം ഉയർന്ന പദവിയിൽ വിലയിരുത്തുന്നു. ജീവനിൽ അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് വളരെ ആസക്തനാണെന്നും, ആനപ്പുറത്തിരുന്ന് ഇന്ദ്രനെപ്പോലെ ഭഗദത്തൻ പൊരുതുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.164; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"रथातिरथसंख्यापर्व","titleEn":"Rathatirathasankhya Parva (Counting the warriors)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"शकुनिर्मातुलस्तेऽसौ रथ एको नराधिप ।\nप्रसज्य पाण्डवैर्वैरं योत्स्यते नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your maternal uncle Shakuni is one chariot-warrior, lord of men; he will fight, pressing his enmity with the Pandavas, without doubt."}},{"n":2,"text":"एतस्य सैन्या दुर्धर्षाः समरेऽप्रतियायिनः ।\nविकृतायुधभूयिष्ठा वायुवेगसमा जवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"His troops are hard to resist in battle, unrivaled, mostly with odd weapons and fast as the wind."}},{"n":3,"text":"द्रोणपुत्रो महेष्वासः सर्वेषामति धन्विनाम् ।\nसमरे चित्रयोधी च दृढास्त्रश्च महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son, the great archer, is above all archers; in battle he fights in varied ways and is a great chariot-warrior with firm weapons."}},{"n":4,"text":"एतस्य हि महाराज यथा गाण्डीवधन्वनः ।\nशरासनाद्विनिर्मुक्ताः संसक्ता यान्ति सायकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His arrows, great king, like those of the wielder of Gandiva, fly out of his bow joined one to another."}},{"n":5,"text":"नैष शक्यो मया वीरः संख्यातुं रथसत्तमः ।\nनिर्दहेदपि लोकांस्त्रीनिच्छन्नेष महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot count this hero, best of chariot-warriors; this greatly renowned man could burn up the three worlds if he chose."}},{"n":6,"text":"क्रोधस्तेजश्च तपसा संभृतोऽऽश्रमवासिना ।\nद्रोणेनानुगृहीतश्च दिव्यैरस्त्रैरुदारधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His fury and energy were gathered through austerity by one who dwelt in a hermitage, and the noble-minded one has been favored with divine weapons by Drona."}},{"n":7,"text":"दोषस्त्वस्य महानेको येनैष भरतर्षभ ।\nन मे रथो नातिरथो मतः पार्थिवसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"But he has one great fault, best of Bharatas, because of which I count him neither a ratha nor an atiratha, best of kings."}},{"n":8,"text":"जीवितं प्रियमत्यर्थमायुष्कामः सदा द्विजः ।\nन ह्यस्य सदृशः कश्चिदुभयोः सेनयोरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Brahmin loves his life too much and always wishes to live long; yet there is no one like him in either army."}},{"n":9,"text":"हन्यादेकरथेनैव देवानामपि वाहिनीम् ।\nवपुष्मांस्तलघोषेण स्फोटयेदपि पर्वतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a single chariot he could destroy even the army of the gods; with the clap of his hands, he of great frame could split mountains."}},{"n":10,"text":"असंख्येयगुणो वीरः प्रहर्ता दारुणद्युतिः ।\nदण्डपाणिरिवासह्यः कालवत्प्रचरिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of incalculable merits, that hero strikes with terrible brilliance, and will move like Death, unbearable like the staff-bearer, Yama."}},{"n":11,"text":"युगान्ताग्निसमः क्रोधे सिंहग्रीवो महामतिः ।\nएष भारत युद्धस्य पृष्ठं संशमयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In anger he is like the fire at the end of an age, with a lion's neck and great mind; this one, Bharata, will bring the back of the battle to a close."}},{"n":12,"text":"पिता त्वस्य महातेजा वृद्धोऽपि युवभिर्वरः ।\nरणे कर्म महत्कर्ता तत्र मे नास्ति संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His father, of great splendor, though old, is the best even among youths; he will do a great deed in battle, there I have no doubt."}},{"n":13,"text":"अस्त्रवेगानिलोद्धूतः सेनाकक्षेन्धनोत्थितः ।\nपाण्डुपुत्रस्य सैन्यानि प्रधक्ष्यति जये धृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fanned by the wind of his weapons, rising on the fuel of the dry grass of armies, Drona, fixed on victory, will burn the Pandava army."}},{"n":14,"text":"रथयूथपयूथानां यूथपः स नरर्षभः ।\nभारद्वाजात्मजः कर्ता कर्म तीव्रं हिताय वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That bull among men, son of Bharadvaja, leader of the leaders of the herds of chariot-fighters, will do fierce work for your good."}},{"n":15,"text":"सर्वमूर्धाभिषिक्तानामाचार्यः स्थविरो गुरुः ।\nगच्छेदन्तं सृञ्जयानां प्रियस्त्वस्य धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That teacher, old and venerable, who is the guru of all anointed kings, may come to the end of the Srinjayas, but Dhananjaya is dear to him."}},{"n":16,"text":"नैष जातु महेष्वासः पार्थमक्लिष्टकारिणम् ।\nहन्यादाचार्यकं दीप्तं संस्मृत्य गुणनिर्जितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great archer would never kill Partha, who does his work without hardship, remembering his blazing quality, for he has been won over by Arjuna's virtues."}},{"n":17,"text":"श्लाघत्येष सदा वीरः पार्थस्य गुणविस्तरैः ।\nपुत्रादभ्यधिकं चैव भारद्वाजोऽनुपश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hero always praises Partha for his many virtues, and Bharadvaja's son regards him as more than a son."}},{"n":18,"text":"हन्यादेकरथेनैव देवगन्धर्वदानवान् ।\nएकीभूतानपि रणे दिव्यैरस्त्रैः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alone in one chariot that mighty man could kill gods, gandharvas and danavas, even united in battle, with divine weapons."}},{"n":19,"text":"पौरवो राजशार्दूलस्तव राजन्महारथः ।\nमतो मम रथो वीर परवीररथारुजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Paurava, tiger among kings, is your great chariot-warrior, king; I count him a ratha, hero, who breaks the chariots of enemy heroes."}},{"n":20,"text":"स्वेन सैन्येन सहितः प्रतपञ्शत्रुवाहिनीम् ।\nप्रधक्ष्यति स पाञ्चालान्कक्षं कृष्णगतिर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Together with his own army he will scorch the enemy's host and burn the Panchalas as fire driven by the wind burns dry grass."}},{"n":21,"text":"सत्यव्रतो रथवरो राजपुत्रो महारथः ।\nतव राजन्रिपुबले कालवत्प्रचरिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyavrata, best of chariot-warriors, a prince and great chariot-warrior, will move like Death among your enemy's forces, king."}},{"n":22,"text":"एतस्य योधा राजेन्द्र विचित्रकवचायुधाः ।\nविचरिष्यन्ति संग्रामे निघ्नन्तः शात्रवांस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"His warriors, king of kings, with varied armor and weapons, will range in battle slaughtering your foes."}},{"n":23,"text":"वृषसेनो रथाग्र्यस्ते कर्णपुत्रो महारथः ।\nप्रधक्ष्यति रिपूणां ते बलानि बलिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrishasena, son of Karna, is your foremost chariot-warrior and great chariot-warrior; best of the strong, he will burn the enemy's forces."}},{"n":24,"text":"जलसंधो महातेजा राजन्रथवरस्तव ।\nत्यक्ष्यते समरे प्राणान्मागधः परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jalasandha, of great splendor, is your best chariot-warrior, king; the Magadha, slayer of enemy heroes, will give up his life in battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"एष योत्स्यति संग्रामे गजस्कन्धविशारदः ।\nरथेन वा महाबाहुः क्षपयञ्शत्रुवाहिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He will fight in the battle, skilled on elephant back, or in a chariot, mighty-armed, destroying the enemy's host."}},{"n":26,"text":"रथ एष महाराज मतो मम नरर्षभः ।\nत्वदर्थे त्यक्ष्यति प्राणान्सह सैन्यो महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I count this bull among men a chariot-warrior, great king; he will give his life for you in the great battle, with his army."}},{"n":27,"text":"एष विक्रान्तयोधी च चित्रयोधी च संगरे ।\nवीतभीश्चापि ते राजञ्शात्रवैः सह योत्स्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is a valiant fighter and a varied fighter in the battle, and, fearless, will fight your enemies, king."}},{"n":28,"text":"बाह्लीकोऽतिरथश्चैव समरे चानिवर्तिता ।\nमम राजन्मतो युद्धे शूरो वैवस्वतोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahlika is an atiratha, never turning back in battle; I regard him, king, as a hero like Vaivasvata."}},{"n":29,"text":"न ह्येष समरं प्राप्य निवर्तेत कथंचन ।\nयथा सततगो राजन्नाभिहत्य परान्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once he enters battle he would never in any way turn back, like the ever-moving wind, king, without having struck the foe."}},{"n":30,"text":"सेनापतिर्महाराज सत्यवांस्ते महारथः ।\nरणेष्वद्भुतकर्मा च रथः पररथारुजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your commander Satyavan, great king, is a great chariot-warrior, of marvelous deeds in battles, breaker of enemy chariots."}},{"n":31,"text":"एतस्य समरं दृष्ट्वा न व्यथास्ति कथंचन ।\nउत्स्मयन्नभ्युपैत्येष परान्रथपथे स्थितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his battle, there is no distress at all; smiling, he goes against enemies who stand in his chariot's path."}},{"n":32,"text":"एष चारिषु विक्रान्तः कर्म सत्पुरुषोचितम् ।\nकर्ता विमर्दे सुमहत्त्वदर्थे पुरुषोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of men, valiant against his foes, will perform in the clash a very great deed worthy of a good man, for your sake."}},{"n":33,"text":"अलायुधो राक्षसेन्द्रः क्रूरकर्मा महाबलः ।\nहनिष्यति परान्राजन्पूर्ववैरमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alayudha, king of the rakshasas, of cruel deeds and great strength, will kill the enemy, king, remembering his old enmity."}},{"n":34,"text":"एष राक्षससैन्यानां सर्वेषां रथसत्तमः ।\nमायावी दृढवैरश्च समरे विचरिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is the best chariot-warrior of all the rakshasa armies, a master of illusion, firm in hatred, and will range through the battle."}},{"n":35,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषाधिपो वीरो भगदत्तः प्रतापवान् ।\nगजाङ्कुशधरश्रेष्ठो रथे चैव विशारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhagadatta, the brave and mighty lord of Pragjyotisha, the best of those who wield the elephant goad and skilled in the chariot too."}},{"n":36,"text":"एतेन युद्धमभवत्पुरा गाण्डीवधन्वनः ।\nदिवसान्सुबहून्राजन्नुभयोर्जयगृद्धिनोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago he fought with the wielder of Gandiva for very many days, O king, both eager for victory."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः सखायं गान्धारे मानयन्पाकशासनम् ।\nअकरोत्संविदं तेन पाण्डवेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, son of Gandhari, honoring Indra as his friend, he made a pact with that great-souled Pandava."}},{"n":38,"text":"एष योत्स्यति संग्रामे गजस्कन्धविशारदः ।\nऐरावतगतो राजा देवानामिव वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He will fight in the battle, skilled on elephant back, like the king of the gods, Vasava, on Airavata."}}]}]}